  "verbalization": "Hedaol B is shown to have a target relationship with Raji, which is in turn targeted by multiple compounds, including Diosmetin 7-O-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-[Alpha-L-Rhamnopyranosyl-(1->6)]-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside and (1R,3R,4S,7S,9S,11S,13R,14R,15R)-4,11,13,14-tetrahydroxy-7-[(2Z,4R)-4-(hydroxymethyl)hex-2-en-2-yl]-3,9,15-trimethoxy-12,12-dimethyl-6,17-dioxabicyclo[11.3.1]heptadecan-5-one. These compounds are all linked to Carboxylesterase 2, suggesting a potential mechanism by which they interact with this enzyme. The evidence points to a possible pathway where Hedaol B may target Raji, which is then a target of these compounds, and ultimately, these compounds may inhibit Carboxylesterase 2. The integration of these paths suggests that Hedaol B could be a potential inhibitor of Carboxylesterase 2, possibly through a mechanism involving the targeting of Raji, which is a known target of multiple compounds that interact with this enzyme. The evidence supports a possible dependency on the enzyme, but the exact mechanism remains to be clarified.",
